## Objectif

Empêcher toute augmentation de la dette de compatibilité wxPython historique pendant la migration Python 3 / Phoenix.

## État mesuré

L’inventaire Frankenstein recense actuellement :

- 211 branches `"phoenix" in wx.PlatformInfo` ;
- 91 fichiers concernés ;
- aucune branche `six.PY2`, `sys.version_info == 2` ou `"phoenix" not in wx.PlatformInfo` active.

## Modifications

- ajoute un test automatisé basé sur l’inventaire existant ;
- plafonne les branches Phoenix à 211 occurrences et 91 fichiers ;
- refuse le retour des autres branches de compatibilité Python 2 / wxPython Classic déjà supprimées ;
- laisse toute réduction future passer automatiquement sans modifier le plafond immédiatement.

## Effet attendu

La dette existante peut uniquement rester stable ou diminuer. Toute nouvelle branche de compatibilité fera échouer la CI.

## Risques

Faibles : aucun code métier n’est modifié. Le test réutilise l’outil d’inventaire déjà exécuté dans le workflow Frankenstein.

## 1. Objetivo

Atualizar o Next.js da versão 16.1.1 para a versão corrigida 16.2.11 antes da implementação da E12.4.3.

## 2. Escopo

- atualiza `next` para `16.2.11`;
- atualiza `eslint-config-next` para `16.2.11`;
- regenera o `package-lock.json` de forma direcionada;
- não altera código, banco, rotas, documentação funcional, workflow ou infraestrutura permanente.

## 3. Arquivos finais

- `package.json`;
- `package-lock.json`.

## 4. Validação

- `npm ci --ignore-scripts`: aprovado no fluxo isolado usado para regenerar o lockfile;
- `npm run check`: aprovado no mesmo fluxo, antes da publicação do lockfile;
- Security Checks: aprovado;
- previews Vercel `lp-factory-10` e `lpf-10-services`: aprovados;
- diff final restrito aos dois arquivos de dependências;
- workflow temporário removido antes do fechamento do PR.

## 5. Fonte

- Next.js July 2026 Security Release: `16.2.11` indicada como versão Active LTS corrigida para a linha 16.x.

## 6. Estado

Atualização pronta para revisão e merge humano. Depois do merge, a branch da E12.4.3 deve incorporar a `main` atualizada antes de iniciar código, Admin Dashboard ou banco.

## Summary

Completes the Mercurial R0 upstream model in Mercurial-native terms, without extracting a generic SCM interface. It preserves portable changeset identity separately from clone-local revision numbers, file revisions and copy metadata, manifests and flags, heads/bookmarks/branches/tags, phase and publishing behavior, subrepositories, evolution markers, repository requirements, and partial availability.

A separate wet witness creates a real Mercurial repository through typed argv and filesystem effects, reads its native facts back, constructs the canonical projection from those observations, and requires `mercurial_decode_projection` to accept it. R0 remains read-only: no conditional-advance claim is fabricated before an executing transaction transport exists.

## What changed

- pin every Mercurial external-authority anchor to the immutable 7.2.3 release archive;
- model changesets, manifests, file revisions, copy-source provenance, and raw path octets independently;
- decode raw node-identity text into an exact structural 20-octet carrier, refusing empty, short, non-hexadecimal, or uppercase wire values before canonical repository state exists;
- preserve heads, bookmarks, named branches, versioned/local tags, subrepositories, and optional evolution markers;
- preserve public/draft/secret phases and publishing versus non-publishing exchange behavior;
- refuse duplicate identities, missing undeclared references, unknown flags/phases, incomplete phase assignments, and phase-monotonicity violations;
- represent complete, partial, and inaccessible projections as distinct construction-time arms so inaccessible observations have no repository-fact payload; keep decoded complete and partial repositories distinct and refuse present-plus-declared-missing identities;
- compare caller-supplied read-back observations and reject a perturbed observation;
- execute a real three-changeset/two-head Mercurial fixture as typed process/file operations, decode its emitted changeset/manifest/file-revision identities, construct a full projection with observed requirements/topology/phase/file facts, and pass that projection through the canonical decoder;
- keep write/conditional-advance capability explicitly unavailable at R0.

## Why

Mercurial deliberately differs from Git: local revision numbers are not portable identities, bookmarks are not named branches, phases affect exchange, and copy provenance belongs to file history. Modeling those differences before R1 prevents Git vocabulary from becoming the accidental common interface.

## Validation

- all 26 pure Mercurial upstream-model witnesses — PASS
- real Mercurial 7.2.3 typed-effect canonical-projection/decode witness in wet mode — PASS
- cargo fmt --all --check — PASS
- git diff --check — PASS

## Boundary

No ScmKind, vendor switch, common target/ref carrier, semantic integration rule, forge transport, or hosted-product promise is introduced. R1 remains gated on Git, Mercurial, and Pijul R0 receipts.
